cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use GRABNES, please cite the software using the metadata below,
  together with the exact version or Git commit that you used.
type: software
title: "GRABNES: Graphene and Boron Nitride Electronic Structure"
abstract: >-
  GRABNES is a Fortran code for real-space tight-binding calculations of the
  electronic structure and quantum transport of graphene, hexagonal boron
  nitride, and the layered and moire systems built from them. It constructs
  atomistic Hamiltonians and solves them by exact diagonalization (band
  structures, densities of states) or by Lanczos recursion on large cells.
authors:
